##############################################################
# SPEYCU - specific actions of the Classic object YCU (external customer codes)
#
# Purpose
#   VERIF_CRE / VERIF_MOD (before the transaction): refuse the record with
#   OK = 0 when the VAT number is empty or the linked X3 customer is unknown.
#   INICRE / INIMOD (inside the transaction, just before Write / Rewrite):
#   normalise the VAT number in [F:YCU]; GOK = 0 would abort the transaction.
#
# Prerequisites
#   - GESATB: table YCUSTEXT, abbreviation YCU, index YCU0 on YCODE;
#     fields YCODE (key), YNAME, YVATNUM, BPCNUM (optional link to BPCUSTOMER)
#   - GESAMK: screen YCU0 holding YCODE, YNAME, YVATNUM, BPCNUM
#   - GESAOB: object YCU on table YCUSTEXT (its specific actions are looked up
#     in script SPE + object code = SPEYCU)
#   - TXT: chapter 160 (specific messages), message 11 "VAT number required",
#     message 12 "Unknown customer"
#   - One X/Y/Z activity code on every element above (GESACV)
#
# Notes
#   - The VERIF_CRE help page documents only OK = 0. GMESSAGE carries the text
#     as in classic-objects.md (SPEBPC example); check how your patch level
#     displays it before relying on it.
#   - Actions are reached by Gosub: they share the locals of the object
#     process, so the checks live in Funprogs with their own Local File.
#
# References: classic-objects.md, screens-and-masks.md, conventions-and-naming.md
##############################################################

$ACTION
  Case ACTION
    When "VERIF_CRE" : Gosub Y_VERIF
    When "VERIF_MOD" : Gosub Y_VERIF
    When "INICRE"    : Gosub Y_NORMALISE
    When "INIMOD"    : Gosub Y_NORMALISE
  Endcase
Return

$Y_VERIF
  # No transaction yet: the entered values are in the screen class [M:YCU0]
  If vireblc([M:YCU0]YVATNUM, 4) = ""
    GMESSAGE = mess(11, 160, 1)
    OK = 0
  Elsif [M:YCU0]BPCNUM <> "" and func SPEYCU.Y_CUSTOMER_EXISTS([M:YCU0]BPCNUM) = 0
    GMESSAGE = mess(12, 160, 1)
    OK = 0
  Endif
Return

$Y_NORMALISE
  # Transaction open, [F:YCU] loaded from the screens: last changes before the write
  [F:YCU]YVATNUM = toupper(vireblc([F:YCU]YVATNUM, 4)) : # no spaces, upper case
Return

##############################################################
# Y_CUSTOMER_EXISTS - 1 when the X3 customer exists, else 0
##############################################################
Funprog Y_CUSTOMER_EXISTS(CUSTNUM)
Value Char CUSTNUM()
Local File BPCUSTOMER [YBPC]
  Look [YBPC]BPC0 = [L]CUSTNUM               : # existence test, buffer untouched
  If fstat = 0
    End 1
  Endif
End 0
